= Heuristic Routing for Rapid Disaster Response Allocation
== Abstract
This paper evaluates lightweight routing heuristics for allocating response units to incident requests under time constraints. The framework offers reproducible comparison and clear operational limitations.

== Method
Greedy + nearest-neighbor routing with response-time scoring.

== Experiments
We run a CPU-only benchmark with fixed seed and report accuracy.

== Limitations
Small synthetic/curated data and simplified metrics reduce external validity.

== Ethical Considerations
The tool is intended for decision support; human oversight is required.
